(6264726, 926509, 83313, '<td valign="top">Very unique wildlife shot! No doubt some people are getting grossed out by this. I''ll bet if you just described it as venison, it wouldn''t have such an effect. But that''s the point, isn''t it?</td>', 'Very unique wildlife shot! No doubt some people are getting grossed out by this. I''ll bet if you just described it as venison, it wouldn''t have such an effect. But that''s the point, isn''t it?', '2010-12-30 14:17:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6264731, 926947, 83313, '<td valign="top">I see you are taking a tip from <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=114969" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Gyaban</a> and trying the selfie route to high scores. Nice work with the lighting. The pose reminds me of some cigarette ads from the 70''s, where it asked you to pick the smoker of that brand (I think it was Salem) out of a crowd of people putting on airs and pretensions. It was always the tall, handsome square-jawed guy with the jacket slung across his shoulder in this manner. I always thought that guy was the fakest of the bunch.<br/> <br/>Ok, extra pointage for sending me off on a retro rabbit trail.<br/> <br/>Added: Found one. It was actually Camel filters. Enjoy.<br/><a href="//www.flickr.com/photos/fugue/3876769041/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//farm4.static.flickr.com/3536/3876769041_ca4a2ffe5f_t.jpg'', strrpos(''//farm4.static.flickr.com/3536/3876769041_ca4a2ffe5f_t.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//farm4.static.flickr.com/3536/3876769041_ca4a2ffe5f_t.jpg"/></a></td>', 'I see you are taking a tip from  Gyaban and trying the selfie route to high scores. Nice work with the lighting. The pose reminds me of some cigarette ads from the 70''s, where it asked you to pick the smoker of that brand (I think it was Salem) out of a crowd of people putting on airs and pretensions. It was always the tall, handsome square-jawed guy with the jacket slung across his shoulder in this manner. I always thought that guy was the fakest of the bunch. Ok, extra pointage for sending me off on a retro rabbit trail. Added: Found one. It was actually Camel filters. Enjoy.', '2010-12-30 14:39:26.000000', NULL, 1),
