(6272262, 927005, 116649, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for the comments, once again items were brought to my attention which I wouldn''t Have considered otherwise.<br/> <br/>Sadly, due to a perfect storm of interruptions I had very little time to post process, but the wallpaper was just removed last week and the room was newly painted, and I didn''t even notice the imperfections. My downfall was the use of the brightest light I own, which happened to be a halogen shop light, thus the yellow cast that I did not correct for.  I am an admitted amature, and need to invest in some proper lighting equipment, but I am here to learn, and continue to do just that.<br/> <br/>This was an experiment I used to do with my kids while studying density, for those interested the layers consist of honey, colored karo corn syrup, Dawn dishwashing detergent, colored water, and olive oil. I was going to add colored alcohol and lamp oil, and even try to light it, but ran out of time!<br/> <br/>Thanks again for the support and constructive criticism, it helps me grow.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-01-05 14:13:16.</i></td>', 'Thank you all for the comments, once again items were brought to my attention which I wouldn''t Have considered otherwise. Sadly, due to a perfect storm of interruptions I had very little time to post process, but the wallpaper was just removed last week and the room was newly painted, and I didn''t even notice the imperfections. My downfall was the use of the brightest light I own, which happened to be a halogen shop light, thus the yellow cast that I did not correct for.  I am an admitted amature, and need to invest in some proper lighting equipment, but I am here to learn, and continue to do just that. This was an experiment I used to do with my kids while studying density, for those interested the layers consist of honey, colored karo corn syrup, Dawn dishwashing detergent, colored water, and olive oil. I was going to add colored alcohol and lamp oil, and even try to light it, but ran out of time! Thanks again for the support and constructive criticism, it helps me grow.', '2011-01-05 13:41:43.000000', '2011-01-05 14:13:16.000000', 0),
